hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1397","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: \"Whoever supplicates Allah to exalt my mention, Allah will send blessings upon him ten times.\" [Muslim] ."
"1398","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The people closest to me on the Day of Resurrection are those who send the most blessings (salawat) upon me.” Al-Tirmidhi narrated it and said it was a good hadith."
"1399","On the authority of Aws bin Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “One of your best days is Friday, so increase sending blessings (salawat) upon me on it, for your blessings upon me are presented to me.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, how can our prayers be presented to you when your body has decayed? He said: He says: “Well done.” He said: “Allah Almighty has forbidden the bodies of the prophets on earth.” [Abu Dawud]"
"1400","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “May the nose of a man be rubbed in dust (i.e., may he be disgraced) in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send blessings (salawat) upon me.” It was narrated by Al-Tirmidhi and he said it was a good hadith."
"1401","On his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not make my grave a festival and pray for me, for your prayers will reach me wherever you are.” [Abu Dawud]"
"1402","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “No one greets me except that Allah returns my soul to me until I return his greeting to him” [Abu Dawud]."
"1403","On the authority of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The miser is the one in whose presence I am mentioned, but he does not pray for me” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1404","On the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard a man supplicating during his prayer. He did not glorify Allah Almighty, nor did he pray for the Prophet (ﷺ). So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Hurry this up.” Then he called him and said to him - or to someone else: If one of you prays, let him begin by praising his Lord, Glory be to Him, and praising Him, then pray for the Prophet (ﷺ). Then he supplicates for whatever he wishes.” [Abu Dawud]"
"1405","The Prophet (ﷺ) came to us and we asked him, \"O Messenger of Allah, we already know how to greet you (i.e., say As-salamu 'alaikum), but how should we supplicate for you?\" He (ﷺ) said, \"Say: 'Allahumma salli 'ala Muhammadin, wa 'ala 'ali Muhammadin, kama sallaita 'ala 'ali Ibrahima, innaka Hamidum Majid. Allahumma barik 'ala Muhammadin, wa 'ala 'ali Muhammadin, kama barakta 'ala 'ali Ibrahima, innaka Hamidum Majid [O Allah, exalt the mention of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as you exalted the family of Ibrahim. You are Praised and Glorious. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed the family of Ibrahim. You are Praised and Glorious.\"' [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"1406","On the authority of Abu Masoud bin Ubadah Al-Badri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to us while we were in the council of Sa’d bin Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him. Bashir bin Saad said to him: Allah Almighty commanded us to pray for you, O Messenger of Allah, so how should we pray for you? The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was silent, until we wished he had not asked him. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Say, O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You bestowed blessings upon the family of Abraham, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious, and peace as you have taught” [Muslim]."
"1407","The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"O Messenger of Allah! How should we supplicate for you?\" He (ﷺ) replied, \"Say: 'Allahumma salli 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala azwajihi wa dhurriyyatihi, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahima; wa barik 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala azwajihi wa dhurriyyatihi, kama barakta 'ala Ibrahima, innaka Hamidum-Majid (O Allah sent Your Salat (O Allah, exalt the mention of Muhammad and his wives and offspring as You exalted the mention of the family of Ibrahim, and bless Muhammad and the wives and the offspring of Muhammad as you blessed the family of Ibrahim. You are the Praised, the Glorious'.\" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
